<!-- CORE FEATURES -->
<section class="gate-section" id="features">
  <div class="gate-container-wide">
    <p class="section-label reveal">Core features</p>
    <div class="gate-features-grid reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.05s;">
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>{{ versions.gate.rules }} Detection Rules</h3>
        <p>Patterns for AWS, GCP, Azure, GitHub, Stripe, AI keys, databases, and private keys, across 25+ providers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Credential Verification</h3>
        <p>Opt-in <code>--verify</code> asks provider APIs whether a matched secret is still live. No network calls unless you pass the flag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Auto-Fix Engine</h3>
        <p>Can move a hardcoded secret into a .env file and rewrite the reference, across 9 languages. Check the diff before committing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Interactive Remediation</h3>
        <p>One keypress per finding to fix, vault, or ignore it, so you can work through a scan in a single pass.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Incident Response</h3>
        <p>5-step guided workflow: rotate credentials, audit access, clean code, scrub history, document.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Compliance Reports</h3>
        <p>Maps findings to OWASP, NIST 800-63B, CIS Benchmark v8, and SOC2 controls. A starting point for an audit, not a substitute for one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>SARIF Output</h3>
        <p>SARIF output for GitHub Advanced Security code scanning alerts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Git History Scanning</h3>
        <p>Scans past commits for secrets and generates purge scripts you can review and run to rewrite history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-feature-card">
        <h3>Zero Config</h3>
        <p>Runs on defaults. No setup file, account, or API key required to start; add a <code>.gaterc</code> when you need one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- GITHUB ACTION -->
<section class="gate-section" id="docs-github-action">
  <div class="gate-container-wide">
    <p class="section-label reveal">CI/CD</p>
    <div class="gate-docs-section reveal">
      <h2 class="gate-docs-heading">GitHub Action</h2>
      <p class="gate-docs-text">Run Gate in CI with the GitHub Action. It scans pull requests and pushes, and uploads SARIF results to GitHub code scanning.</p>

      <div class="gate-gh-action">
        <div class="gate-gh-action-bar">.github/workflows/gate.yml</div>
        <div class="gate-gh-action-body"><span class="kw">name</span>: Gate
<span class="kw">on</span>: [pull_request, push]

<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/gate@v2
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">mode</span>: enforce
          <span class="kw">verify</span>: <span class="val">true</span>
          <span class="kw">format</span>: sarif
          <span class="kw">fail-on</span>: high</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

